.TH LISZT 1 "2026-07-19" "liszt" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
liszt, lz \- list directory contents, byte-identical to GNU ls, faster
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B liszt
.RI [ OPTION ]...
.RI [ FILE ]...
.br
.B lz
.RI [ OPTION ]...
.RI [ FILE ]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B liszt
is a from-scratch C11 reimplementation of GNU
.BR ls (1)
(coreutils 9.11). Under a pinned environment (locale, TZ, COLUMNS,
LS_COLORS, piped stdout) its output is byte-identical to GNU ls on
every supported flag, and faster on every measured workload.
.B lz
is the same binary under a shorter name; it prints
.B liszt
as its program name in version output and diagnostics keep the invoked
name, exactly as GNU ls behaves when renamed.
.PP
The complete GNU ls 9.11 option surface is supported: formats
.RB ( \-l ,
.BR \-C ,
.BR \-x ,
.BR \-m ,
.BR \-1 ),
sorting
.RB ( \-t ,
.BR \-S ,
.BR \-v ,
.BR \-X ,
.BR \-U ,
.BR \-\-sort ),
recursion and dereferencing
.RB ( \-R ,
.BR \-H ,
.BR \-L ),
color and indicators
.RB ( \-\-color ,
.BR \-F ,
.BR \-p ,
.BR \-\-file\-type ),
quoting styles, time words and styles
.RB ( \-\-time ,
.BR \-\-time\-style ,
.BR \-\-full\-time ),
ignore patterns
.RB ( \-\-hide ,
.BR \-I ,
.BR \-B ),
and the oddballs
.RB ( \-\-dired ,
.BR \-\-hyperlink ,
.BR \-\-zero ,
.BR \-Z ,
.BR \-\-author ).
See
.BR ls (1)
for option semantics; they are identical by construction and pinned by
a differential test suite against the reference implementation.
.SH DEVIATIONS
One intentional divergence is carried, with its own regression
registry: GNU ls assigns a rejected display width into an unsigned
type before clamping, so names containing control bytes or invalid
multibyte sequences in multibyte locales can wrap column layout
arithmetic. liszt honors the intended clamp (width 0). Quoted styles
and
.B \-q
are unaffected.
.SH EXTENSIONS
Beyond the GNU surface, liszt offers extensions - all off by default;
with none active, output is byte-identical to GNU ls. Extension long
options match by exact spelling only (no abbreviation).
.TP
.BR \-\-icons [=\fIWHEN\fR]
Prefix each name with a Nerd-Font icon chosen from compiled-in tables
(exact filename, then directory name, then suffix, then file type).
.I WHEN
is
.BR always ,
.BR auto ,
or
.BR never ;
bare
.B \-\-icons
means
.B auto
(icons only when standard output is a terminal). liszt never reads
directory contents to choose a glyph, and with the builtin tables the
stat-less listing plan is preserved. Not combinable with
.B \-\-dired
(positional last-wins, like
.BR \-\-hyperlink ).
.TP
.B \-\-tree
List directory contents as a tree. Implies recursion; the format is
one-per-line unless
.B \-l
is active (metadata on the left, branch glyphs in the name column).
The full sort, ignore, and grouping surface applies to each sibling
list;
.B \-d
wins (no tree);
.B \-\-dired
self-disables. Symbolic links are shown but not descended unless
.B \-L
is given; directory cycles are always detected (exit status 2). One
directory descriptor is open at any moment, at any depth, so deep or
huge trees cannot exhaust descriptors. Unreadable subdirectories are
diagnosed and skipped (exit status 1).
.TP
.BI \-\-level= N
Descend at most
.I N
levels (entries directly in each operand are level 1). Directories at
the boundary are shown, styled, and never entered. 0 or absent means
unlimited. Requires
.BR \-\-tree .
.TP
.BI \-\-tree\-limit= N
Show at most
.I N
entries per directory, applied after sorting; the rest collapse into a
final "... \fIK\fP more" line (plain bytes: no color, indicator, or
icon). Entries hidden by the cap are not descended. 0 or absent means
uncapped. Requires
.BR \-\-tree .
.TP
.BI \-\-tree\-glyphs= WORD
Branch glyph charset:
.BR unicode ,
.BR ascii ,
or
.B auto
(the default: unicode when the locale codeset is UTF-8). Requires
.BR \-\-tree .
.TP
.B \-\-git
Show a two-character git status cell before each name in long format
(silently inert otherwise). Dependency-free: liszt reads the repo's
index directly (formats v2-v4, SHA-256 repos, linked worktrees) and
compares worktree stat data; nothing is ever hashed. The first
character is always
.B \-
(staged state needs object hashing); the second is
.B \-
clean,
.B M
modified,
.B T
type change,
.B N
untracked,
.B I
ignored, or
.B U
conflict. Directories with tracked content show
.B \-\-
without recursing; submodules are never entered. Split-index and
sparse-index repos, and anything malformed, degrade to a blank column
(reasons under
.BR LISZT_DEBUG_GIT=1 ).
Known limits: staged-only changes read as clean; GIT_DIR and
core.excludesFile are not consulted; sizes compare modulo 4 GiB.
.TP
.B \-\-git\-ignore
Hide entries ignored by gitignore rules (nested .gitignore files and
the repository's info/exclude), in any format. Tracked files are
never hidden. Does not imply
.BR \-\-git .
.TP
.B \-\-no\-git
Suppress an earlier
.B \-\-git
(positional, last wins).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
The GNU-compatible variables
.BR LS_COLORS ,
.BR COLUMNS ,
.BR TIME_STYLE ,
.BR TABSIZE ,
.BR LS_BLOCK_SIZE ,
.BR BLOCK_SIZE ,
.BR BLOCKSIZE ,
.B POSIXLY_CORRECT
and the locale variables behave as in
.BR ls (1).
.PP
liszt additionally reads:
.TP
.B LS_ICONS
Icon overrides, LS_COLORS-shaped: colon-separated
.IR key = value
entries where
.I key
is
.BI * .suffix
(case-insensitive),
.IB name /
(exact directory name),
a two-letter LS_COLORS file-type label
.RB ( di ,
.BR fi ,
\&...), or an exact filename. Values take the same backslash escapes
as LS_COLORS; an empty value blanks the icon cell. Unparsable values
diagnose and fall back to the builtin tables.
.TP
.B LISZT_ICONS
Default WHEN for
.B \-\-icons
when the flag is absent.
.TP
.BR LISZT_ICON_SPACING " (fallback " EZA_ICON_SPACING )
Spaces after the glyph, 0-8, default 1.
.TP
.B LISZT_ICONS_OSC66
When 1, wrap each glyph in the kitty text-sizing sequence
(OSC 66, w=1) so supporting terminals render exactly one cell.
.TP
.B LISZT_DEBUG_PLAN
Print the selected sort engine and stat plan to standard error.
.TP
.B LISZT_DEBUG_STATS
Print engine counters (radix passes, comparator calls, time-memo hit
rate) to standard error.
.TP
.B LISZT_DEBUG_VERIFY
Cross-check optimized engines against the scalar reference oracle;
mismatches abort. Used by the test harness on every run.
.TP
.B LISZT_FORCE_SCALAR
Disable optimized sort engines for this run.
.TP
.B LISZT_PARALLEL_MIN
Entry-count threshold for the parallel stat phase (default 400).
Large values force the serial path.
.TP
.B LISZT_PARALLEL_WORKERS
Cap the worker count of the parallel stat phase.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
0
Success.
.TP
1
Minor problems (for example: cannot access a subdirectory).
.TP
2
Serious trouble (for example: cannot access a command-line argument).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B lz \-la
Long listing of the current directory, dotfiles included.
.TP
.B liszt \-\-color=always \-F | less \-R
Colored, classified listing through a pager.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ls (1),
.BR dircolors (1)
.PP
